              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 494,
                "end_index": 574,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "This fee is known as the **expense ratio** (which includes the *management fee*)"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                2,
                3
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 578,
                "end_index": 678,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Unlike hedge funds\u2014which historically charged a \"2 and 20\" fee (2% of assets + 20% of all profits)"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                4,
                5
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 717,
                "end_index": 858,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "In the United States, the SEC generally prohibits mutual funds from charging asymmetric performance fees (taking a percentage of the profits)"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                2,
                6
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 911,
                "end_index": 1025,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "*   **Actively Managed Mutual Funds:** Typically charge a management fee between **0.5% and 1.5%** of AUM annually"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                7
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1027,
                "end_index": 1105,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "The average actively managed equity mutual fund fee is around **0.7% to 1.1%**"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                8
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1108,
                "end_index": 1328,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "*   **Passively Managed Mutual Funds (Index Funds):** Because these funds simply track an index (like the S&P 500) and require no active stock-picking, their fees are much lower, typically ranging from **0.02% to 0.20%**"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                0,
                1
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1331,
                "end_index": 1511,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "*Example: If you invest $10,000 in an active mutual fund with a 1% expense ratio, the management company will deduct $100 over the course of the year to cover their operating costs"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                9,
                10,
                11
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1718,
                "end_index": 1938,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "In reality, **individual mutual fund managers are salaried employees** of the asset management firm (like Fidelity, Vanguard, or BlackRock) and **do not** receive a direct, flat percentage of the fund's assets or profits"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                12
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1941,
                "end_index": 2038,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Instead, their compensation is structured through a combination of salary and performance metrics"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                13,
                14
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2085,
                "end_index": 2214,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "**Base Salary:** Typically ranges from **$150,000 to $1,000,000+** depending on the size of the firm and the manager's experience"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                9,
                5
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2220,
                "end_index": 2349,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "**Performance Bonus (The largest portion):** Roughly 80% of active mutual fund managers have bonuses tied directly to performance"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                9,
                4
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2351,
                "end_index": 2506,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "This is typically calculated using:\n    *   **Benchmark Performance:** Beat a specific benchmark (like the S&P 500) over a 1-year, 3-year, or 5-year period"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                10,
                11
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2512,
                "end_index": 2685,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "*   **AUM Growth:** The bonus increases if the fund's total assets grow, which happens when the manager makes good investments or when new investors pour money into the fund"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                15
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2688,
                "end_index": 2954,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "#### The Relationship Between Fund Revenue and Manager Pay\nAccording to academic research from the National Bureau of Economic Research (NBER) and the Stockholm School of Economics, there is a **concave relationship** between a fund\u2019s revenue and the manager's pay"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                15
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2688,
                "end_index": 3084,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "#### The Relationship Between Fund Revenue and Manager Pay\nAccording to academic research from the National Bureau of Economic Research (NBER) and the Stockholm School of Economics, there is a **concave relationship** between a fund\u2019s revenue and the manager's pay:\n*   A **1% increase** in the total fees a fund generates only increases the individual manager's personal pay by about **0.15%**"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                16,
                7
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3086,
                "end_index": 3242,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "*   The overwhelming majority of the management fee is kept by the parent company to pay for overhead, analysts, marketing, compliance, and corporate profit"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                15
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3286,
                "end_index": 3421,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Because of this structure, a portfolio manager's personal earnings represent a tiny fraction of a percent of the total fund they manage"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                17
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3286,
                "end_index": 3509,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Because of this structure, a portfolio manager's personal earnings represent a tiny fraction of a percent of the total fund they manage:\n*   **Median US Fund Manager Pay:** Around **$462,000** per year (base salary + bonus)"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                17
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3511,
                "end_index": 3578,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "*   **Average (Mean) US Fund Manager Pay:** Around **$1.1 million**"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                14
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3580,
                "end_index": 3733,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "(This figure is skewed higher by top-tier managers at massive funds, who can make **$4 million to $10+ million** annually during highly successful years)"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            }
